# MoarTube Node Environment Configuration

# Application environment: development or production.
# NODE_ENV controls application runtime behavior; it does NOT select the data
# directory. Setting NODE_ENV=production in a source checkout still uses that
# checkout's data folder unless an explicit directory override is provided.
#
# Data directory selection depends on how Node is launched:
# - Source CLI or the normal VS Code launch: <MoarTube-Node source root>/data.
#   Both npm run dev and npm start use this location, regardless of NODE_ENV.
# - Desktop development (Client + Node, Windows/Linux): an isolated profile at
#   <Client source root>/build/desktop/profiles/<platform>-<arch>/development/
#   MoarTube/client_node/node. It does not share the CLI checkout's data.
# - Installed standalone Node: <OS application-data root>/MoarTube/node.
# - Installed Client + Node bundle (Windows/Linux):
#   <OS application-data root>/MoarTube/client_node/node.
# - Docker Node: /data/MoarTube/node, inside the persistent /data volume.
#
# OS application-data roots:
#   Windows: %APPDATA%
#   macOS:   ~/Library/Application Support (standalone Node)
#   Linux:   $XDG_DATA_HOME, or ~/.local/share when XDG_DATA_HOME is unset.
#
# CLI overrides, in priority order (absolute paths required):
# 1. MOARTUBE_DATA_DIR: the exact Node data directory.
# 2. MOARTUBE_DATA_ROOT: a shared parent; appends MoarTube/node, or just node
#    when the supplied directory is already named MoarTube.
# These overrides take precedence over Docker and source/installed defaults.
# Desktop launchers explicitly pass their selected component directories:
# installed desktop honors MOARTUBE_DATA_ROOT; desktop development uses its
# isolated profile (MOARTUBE_DESKTOP_TEST_DATA_DIR can select that profile root).
#
# Settings, local media, SQLite, and process locks use the selected data folder.
# A different folder means a separate data set; old data is not auto-imported.
# db:migrate uses the same selection, but DATABASE_URL explicitly overrides its
# database target. npm start runs the compiled build; rebuild after code changes.
NODE_ENV=development
